abstract: >
  Source code and experimental benchmark artifacts for an authenticated
  context-bound hybrid digital signature framework combining Ed25519 and
  ML-DSA-44. The software evaluates Ed25519, ML-DSA-44, and the hybrid
  configuration using binary datasets of 1 KB, 1 MB, 100 MB, and 1 GB.
  Each measurement is repeated 100 times. The benchmark measures key
  generation time, signing time, verification time, peak memory usage,
  signature size, and signing throughput. For the hybrid configuration,
  Ed25519 and ML-DSA-44 signatures are generated for the same input and
  combined using an AND-based verification policy. Raw measurements and
  aggregated results are exported to CSV files for reproducibility.
